## Appendix B — Methods (summary)

Paired-end whole-exome sequencing aligned to {{ rep.reference_genome }} (bwa-mem2), duplicate-marked and base-recalibrated (GATK BQSR). Per-sample QC gating preceded joint genotyping (GATK HaplotypeCaller → CombineGVCFs → GenotypeGVCFs) with best-practice hard-filtering. Copy-number (CNVkit) and paralog/mapping quality were reviewed. Variants were annotated with Ensembl VEP (consequence, MANE transcript, gnomAD frequencies, SIFT, PolyPhen); finalist variants were re-scored with CADD, REVEL and AlphaMissense. Pedigree-aware Mendelian analysis, segregation, monozygotic-twin concordance and ACMG-style tiering were performed against the {{ rep.panel_name }} gene panel. Pipelines: CallForge (analysis) + FamilyForge (interpretation).

## Limitations & disclaimer

- Where a parent was not sequenced, de-novo status and phase are inferred, not confirmed.
- Population frequencies and some in-silico metrics are bounded by the locally available databases; finalist scores were retrieved from authoritative external sources.
- This is a **research analysis**, not an accredited diagnostic result. Reported variants are candidates pending orthogonal confirmation, functional validation, and formal ACMG classification by an accredited laboratory before any clinical action.
- Whole-exome sequencing does not reliably detect deep-intronic, regulatory, repeat-expansion, balanced structural, or low-level mosaic variants; a negative or single finding does not exclude all genetic causes.

